#!ipxe
# Example iPXE boot script for gokrazy-router (validated on ThinkPad T410i).
#
# This TEXT file is served once iPXE has already been loaded. The initial
# legacy PXE ROM must receive the iPXE UNDI binary, usually named
# undionly.kpxe (configured as services.pxe.legacyBootFile or bootFile).
#
# Place this file in the TFTP root (e.g. /mnt/data/tftpboot/boot.ipxe) and
# set services.pxe.ipxeScript to "boot.ipxe".
#
# Chain to the local netboot.xyz menu script. On failure, drop to the
# iPXE shell instead of returning to the PXE ROM.

dhcp
chain tftp://${next-server}/netboot.xyz.ipxe ||
shell
